[font_size=19][b]3. Add Ink Hammer to Claude[/b][/font_size]
In the Claude desktop app open [b][color=#efe3c6]Settings > Developer > Edit Config[/color][/b]. That opens [code][color=#efe3c6]claude_desktop_config.json[/color][/code].

Put this in the file, with your own Windows user name and Ink Hammer folder in the two paths (every backslash written twice). The guide in your browser (Help > User guide) can fill them in for you.

[table=1][cell bg=#26282d padding=12,8,12,8][code]{
  "mcpServers": {
    "ink-hammer": {
      "command": "C:\\Users\\you\\.local\\bin\\uv.exe",
      "args": [lb]"run", "--no-project", "--quiet", "C:\\Users\\you\\Documents\\Ink Hammer\\mcp\\ink_hammer_mcp.py"[rb]
    }
  }
}[/code][/cell][/table]

If the file already has an [code]"mcpServers"[/code] section, add only the [code]"ink-hammer": {...}[/code] part inside it, with a comma between it and the entry before.
